<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Bartians</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1274 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian people of the land of Barta in the upper Łyna valley, conquered by the Teutonic Order after long resistance in the 13th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bartians inhabited Barta, an inland Prussian territory around modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartoszyce">Bartoszyce</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, divided into Greater and Lesser Barta. They are known mainly from the chronicle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-dusburg">Peter of Dusburg</a>, written in the 14th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They lived in farming communities ruled by local nobles with fortified places, and shared the religion and language of the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-prussians">Prussians</a>. Their territory lay between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-warmia">Warmia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natangians">Natangia</a> and the Galindian wilderness.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> subdued Barta around 1240 and built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartoszyce">Bartenstein</a>. The Bartians rose in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a> from 1260 under their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwanus">Diwanus</a>, besieging Order castles, but by 1274 they were defeated. Their land became part of the Order's state, and the people merged into the Prussian peasantry.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bartians.jpg" alt="Bartians" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: JakaśKreatywnaNazwa123 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barcja_na_mapie_adm._Polski_i_Rosji.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1274 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Diwanus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Prussian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a>, <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Barta, Bartia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1037&amp;focus=bartians" aria-label="Bartians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5119 381 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bartians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5439 637h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5439 637h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Poland. <a href="/atlas?year=1037&amp;focus=bartians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

